<%#
  Shown wherever email is being set up, when the site has no address to send
  from. Roe has none of its own to fall back on — Postmark rejects any From it
  hasn't verified — so without this every send fails, and the only trace is a
  line in the log the member who tried can't read.

  Same reasoning as the Fly sign-in banner on the deploy page: saying so at
  setup costs nothing, finding out from a failed sign-in costs someone else.

  One partial for both pages so the two warnings can't drift apart.
%>
<% if !SiteSender.configured? %>
  <div class="mb-4 border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 p-4" data-sender-warning>
    <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-amber-900 mb-1">Roe needs an email address</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-amber-800 mb-3">
      Roe sends emails to members (sign-in links, newsletters, etc.) These emails come from
      the author email in Roe's settings. Until you add one, no emails can be sent from Roe.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-amber-800">
      <%= link_to "Add an Author Email in Site settings →", admin_edit_site_config_path,
                  class: "underline font-medium" %>
    </p>
  </div>

<%# Address set, but Postmark refused it. A different problem with a different
    fix, and it can only be discovered by attempting a send — listing Sender
    Signatures needs an Account API token and Roe holds only a Server token. So
    this appears once a send has actually been refused, either by the Send test
    email button or by a real one failing. %>
<% elsif PostmarkConfig.current&.sender_rejected? %>
  <div class="mb-4 border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 p-4  text-amber-800" data-sender-warning data-sender-rejected>
    <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-amber-900 mb-1">Postmark won't send from this email address</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-amber-800 mb-3">
      The Author Email in Roe: <code class="font-mono text-xs"><%= SiteSender.address %></code> has to be confirmed by Postmark as a Sender Signature in order to send emails. Either:
      <ul class="list-disc text-xs pl-4 mb-4">
        <li>Add and confirm the above email as a Sender Signature in Postmark.</li>
        <li>Update your Author Email in <%= link_to "Site Settings", admin_edit_site_config_path,
                    class: "underline font-medium" %> to match the email you've set up in Postmark.</li>
        <ul class="list-disc mt-2">
          <li>Then send a test email below to verify.</li>
        </ul>
      </ul>
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-amber-800 mb-3">
      Postmark response: <em><%= PostmarkConfig.current.sender_error %></em>
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-amber-800">
      <%= link_to "Open Postmark settings →", admin_edit_newsletters_config_path,
                  class: "underline font-medium" %>
    </p>
  </div>
<% end %>
